{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@attached"},{"kind":"text","text":"(extension, conformances: "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events5EventP","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","text":"Event"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence13BinaryCodableP","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/BinaryCodable","text":"BinaryCodable"},{"kind":"text","text":", names: named(name), named(consentCategory), named(schemaVersion), named(schema), named(constraintViolation), named(encode(to:)), named(init(from:)), named(requireBinaryCodable), named(binaryCodableRequirements)) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Event"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"name"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"consent"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events15ConsentCategoryV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","text":"ConsentCategory"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"version"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1)"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"name","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The name destinations record the event under, a string literal; the type’s name when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"consent","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The purpose the event is collected for; "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"name":"version","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The schema version, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":": a positive integer literal, raised for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each breaking change; 1 by default."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"code":["import EventMacros","","@Event(name: \"signed_up\", consent: .functional, version: 2)","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: String","    var seats: Int?","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The macro adds an extension holding:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"static var name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when ","type":"text"},{"code":"name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is given; otherwise the type’s name, ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s default.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static var consentCategory"},{"type":"text","text":", when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"consent"},{"type":"text","text":" is given; otherwise "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static var schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":", when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" is given; otherwise 1, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event"},{"type":"text","text":"’s default."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static var schema"},{"type":"text","text":": an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema"},{"type":"text","text":" with the event’s name, version and each stored"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property’s name, type as written, optionality, whether it has a default value and validation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keywords (its "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" type’s rule’s, then those "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Constrained(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" declares), in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declaration order."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"constraintViolation()"},{"type":"text","text":", when a property declares constraints with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Constrained(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first property, in declaration order, whose value breaks one, which a tracker rejects."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which write a CBOR map of the stored properties, each under"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its name, in declaration order, and read each back by its name, as a hand-written conformance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"would. An optional property missing from the map reads as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":", and one with a default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value as that value. A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" property goes through its own conformance, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only a store’s encoder writes its value."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every stored instance property is encoded, and needs a type annotation. Static and computed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties are left out, and so is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"let"},{"text":" with an initial value, which every value shares.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The struct keeps its memberwise initializer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A stored property whose type isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryCodable"},{"type":"text","text":" is a compile error naming it:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static method 'requireBinaryCodable(bad:)' requires that 'Foo' conform to 'BinaryCodable'"},{"type":"text","text":" for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a property "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bad"},{"type":"text","text":" of type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Foo"},{"type":"text","text":". Applying the macro to anything but a struct, a property with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type annotation, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lazy"},{"type":"text","text":" property, a destructuring pattern, a name that isn’t a non-empty string"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"literal and a version that isn’t a positive integer literal are compile errors too."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Changing an event","level":2,"anchor":"Changing-an-event"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store may still hold records written before an event’s stored properties changed: an app"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"updates with records on disk it hasn’t delivered. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" counts the changes those records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can’t be read through, and only those. Each record carries the version it was stored at, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store drops one stored at another version than the type’s now without reading it, reporting the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event and both versions ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DropReport.versionMismatch"},{"type":"text","text":"). A tracking plan’s check"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlans"},{"type":"text","text":") fails on a change that needs a new version while the version stayed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same, naming the event, the property and the change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These changes are compatible. Keep the version, and the records stored before the change are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"read by each property’s name, in any order:"}]},{"code":["\/\/ Version 1, as released.","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\")","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var screen: String","}","","\/\/ Still version 1: a record stored above reads with coupon nil, currency \"USD\" and screen","\/\/ skipped.","@Event(name: \"checkout_started\")","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Int","    var coupon: String?          \/\/ an optional property added: nil","    var currency: String = \"USD\" \/\/ a property with a default value added: the default","                                 \/\/ screen removed: its stored value is skipped","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"These changes are breaking. Raise the version with each, and the records stored at the earlier","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one are dropped and reported:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@Event(name: \"checkout_started\", version: 2)","struct CheckoutStarted {","    var cartSize: Double  \/\/ a property's type changed (it was Int)","    var coupon: String    \/\/ an optional property made required (it was String?)","    var paymentMethod: String \/\/ a required property added, with no default value","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A version raised for a change whose bytes would still read, such as a property that keeps its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type but changes its meaning, drops the earlier records all the same, so they are never read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as the new shape. Records are never migrated from one version to another.","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/EventMacros\/documentation\/EventMacros\/Event(name:consent:version:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11EventMacros0A04name7consent7versionySSSg_6Events15ConsentCategoryVSgSitcfm","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Event"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"name"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"consent"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events15ConsentCategoryV","text":"ConsentCategory"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"version"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"Event(name:consent:version:)","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Trafflu